;; Waiting on file descriptors (HES61 (a), doc/haskell/HASKELL-EVAL-SURVEY.md "As built: HE6's second half"): waitRead#
;; and waitWrite# block the thread, interruptibly, until its descriptor is ready, as the non-threaded RTS's blocked_queue
;; and awaitEvent do: the scheduler polls the waiting descriptors after the threads' slices (at most every pollEvery) and,
;; when no thread can run, sleeps in poll(2) until one is ready or the first delay expires; a killThread takes the thread
;; off its wait (unblock). The descriptors are the posix layer's host files (pipes, spawned processes' ends); crt's are
;; always ready (its files never block), as its poll says.


